pub fn title -> String = "Run your first program"
pub fn summary -> String =
  "Install Seseragi, check the types in your own main.ssrg, and print a line in the terminal. You do not need a repository checkout or knowledge of Rust."
pub fn scopeTitle -> String = "The environment verified for this guide"
pub fn scope -> String =
  "On October 1, 2026, we verified the published Seseragi 0.61.19 release and Bun 1.3.9 on Linux x64 (Debian 13, glibc 2.41), in a new working directory. The check used an empty home directory and an explicit PATH, with no Rust, Cargo, or existing project. Seseragi is experimental; compatibility with future releases is not guaranteed."
pub fn platformTitle -> String = "1. Choose the installation steps for your OS"
pub fn platform -> String =
  "Choose one path matching your OS and CPU. After installation, every platform uses the same main.ssrg program and the same lint and run commands. These published archives are precompiled, so you do not need Rust or Cargo."
pub fn prerequisites -> String =
  "Have a text editor and network access to bun.com and GitHub available. The installation locations below belong to your user account. These steps do not use administrator privileges or npm install."
pub fn otherPlatformsTitle -> String = "Verification scope"
pub fn otherPlatforms -> String =
  "Linux x64 was tested from installation through execution. The macOS and Windows commands are based on published archives and official installation instructions, but were not executed in this verification. If the OS displays a security warning, check the official download source and OS guidance rather than ignoring the warning."
pub fn bunTitle -> String = "Install on Linux x64 (execution verified)"
pub fn bun -> String =
  "Bun runs the program generated by Seseragi. We pin the verified version, 1.3.9, here. Its official installation script installs into .bun in your home directory. PATH is the list of directories your terminal searches for commands; export adds Bun to that list. The final command should print 1.3.9."
pub fn cli -> String =
  "Download the Linux x64 archive and checksum from GitHub Releases. Continue to tar only if sha256sum reports OK. The destination is .local/opt/seseragi/0.61.19 inside your home directory. This is a precompiled release, so Rust is unnecessary. The CLI includes the runtime needed for the single-file program below; you do not need to download a separate runtime archive."
pub fn cliCaption -> String = "Install the Linux x64 release"
pub fn versionCaption -> String = "Expected version output"
pub fn path -> String =
  "The PATH settings apply only to the current terminal. Continue in the same terminal. If a new terminal cannot find the commands, use the PATH recovery step below. To keep the setting, save it in your shell's configuration file."
pub fn fileTitle -> String = "2. Create your own file"
pub fn directory -> String =
  "Create a new hello-seseragi directory outside any repository or existing Seseragi project. Choose another name if it already exists. Run all remaining commands inside this directory."
pub fn file -> String =
  "Use your text editor to create main.ssrg in this directory and save the following line. The filename must end in .ssrg, without an extra .txt. This minimal example needs neither package.json nor seseragi.toml."
pub fn reading -> String =
  "main names the function where execution begins. pub makes it available as the entry point. effect fn declares a function that performs operations such as printing. The expression after = is its body. Passing the string to println with a space prints the string and a newline. You only need these parts of the syntax for this first run."
pub fn checkTitle -> String = "3. Check the types, then run"
pub fn lint -> String =
  "First, use lint to check for syntax and type errors. Success produces no output and exits with code 0. This does not execute the program, so it does not print Hello, Seseragi! yet."
pub fn lintCaption -> String = "Check the types (no output on success)"
pub fn run -> String =
  "Next, use run to execute it. The CLI compiles the source and starts the generated program with Bun. This program prints in your terminal; it does not start a web server."
pub fn runCaption -> String = "Run in the same directory"
pub fn outputCaption -> String = "Terminal output (with a trailing newline)"
pub fn success -> String =
  "If you see this line and the command finishes without an error, it worked. Change the text inside the quotes, save the file, and run the same command again to change the output."
pub fn recoveryTitle -> String = "If something goes wrong"
pub fn missingCommand -> String =
  "For seseragi: command not found, or a failure to launch the Bun target adapter, restore PATH with the commands for your OS below. Check that paths for both executables are printed. If either is missing, return to its installation step."
pub fn pathCaption -> String = "Restore PATH in this terminal"
pub fn wrongFile -> String =
  "For lint path does not exist, use cd to enter the directory where you saved main.ssrg. For an error mentioning .ssrg source file, check that your editor did not name it main.ssrg.txt. If main must be public appears, restore pub at the start of the example."
pub fn badSource -> String =
  "SES-T0101 reports a type mismatch: for example, assigning a string to a value annotated Int. Read the filename, line number, expected type, and actual type in the diagnostic, then correct the value or annotation. For your first run, save the exact line above again and pass lint before running it."
pub fn badArchive -> String =
  "If checksum verification fails, stop before extraction or execution and download both the archive and .sha256 from the same release again. For Exec format error, check the OS and CPU selection. For a GLIBC version error, check the Linux system requirement."
pub fn nextTitle -> String = "Next, write values and functions"
pub fn next -> String =
  "Start by naming a value, then declare a function with types and call it. Each article explains the notation you need."
pub fn web -> String =
  "To make a web app, follow the separate project walkthrough for project creation, VS Code, the development server, and a production build."
pub fn bunLink -> String = "Official Bun installation instructions"
pub fn releaseLink -> String = "Seseragi 0.61.19 release assets"
pub fn archiveLink -> String = "Archive installation steps for each OS"
pub fn webLink -> String = "Create a local web app"

pub fn linuxRequirements -> String =
  "Use bash on Linux x64 with glibc 2.34 or later. uname should show Linux x86_64; getconf shows your glibc version. There is no archive for musl systems such as Alpine, or Linux ARM64. You need bash, curl, unzip, tar, and sha256sum. Install missing tools with your operating system's package manager."

pub fn macTitle -> String = "Install on macOS (source-checked, not executed)"

pub fn macBody -> String =
  "Bun's installation guidance requires macOS 13 or later. Run uname -m in your terminal: arm64 means Apple Silicon; x86_64 means an Intel Mac. The target below selects Apple Silicon. On Intel, change it to target=darwin-x64 before running the commands. These steps use curl, bash, unzip, tar, and shasum."

pub fn macCli -> String =
  "Install Bun first, then Seseragi in the same terminal. Extraction proceeds only after checksum verification. The final output should begin with seseragi 0.61.19 and include release. Its target value depends on your Mac's CPU."

pub fn windowsTitle -> String = "Install on Windows x64 (source-checked, not executed)"

pub fn windowsBody -> String =
  "Bun's installation guidance requires Windows 10 version 1809 or later. Use PowerShell. After installing Bun, this block extracts the Windows x64 release inside your user account's LOCALAPPDATA directory. There is no Seseragi archive for Windows ARM64. Use this block rather than mixing it with the Linux or macOS shell commands."

pub fn windowsResult -> String =
  "Check that Bun prints 1.3.9 and Seseragi prints a line beginning with seseragi 0.61.19 that includes release. If SHA-256 checksum mismatch appears, stop and check the downloaded files."

pub fn unixCaption -> String = "Linux or macOS terminal"

pub fn windowsCaption -> String = "Windows PowerShell"
